From 42289f2a94056ed70b8bf469af6745fbdd86a3bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:16:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(v2): reuse config-handler artifacts across chat folders
 via a process cache

First-message-drop F5c. OMO's config handler owned 11.7s of a 17.7s cold
plugin setup (66%, app-layer addendum B.5), and every folder rebuild re-paid
it although plugin components, agents, global commands and the Claude Code
MCP configs are identical for every (empty) chat folder. New process-level
cache (globalThis + registered symbol, survives module re-imports):
 - plugin components keyed by the claude_code config slice + a fingerprint of
   the ~/.claude plugin roots (install/uninstall invalidates); retryable load
   failures are never cached;
 - the agent-config snapshot hoisted from the per-instance closure to a
   process map keyed by the OpenCode config slice + a fingerprint of the
   folder's project sources; folders with none of those sources (every chat
   folder) share one snapshot, folders with project content stay per-folder;
 - directory-independent command sources (builtin commands/skills, user and
   global commands/skills) memoized; project sources still load per folder;
 - loadMcpConfigs memoized on a ~/.claude.json fingerprint; cwd-bound builtin
   MCPs still rebuild per folder.
Escape hatch: OMO_DISABLE_PROCESS_CONFIG_CACHE=1 restores per-call loads.
test-setup resets the caches per test.
